<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύσιμος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to loose</i> or <i>relieve</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					811
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>that can be redeemed, redeemable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέχυρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					820e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that can be solved, refutable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συλλογισμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>APr.</u>
					70a31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ λ. τῶν νόμων</span> the legal texts
			read by fourth-year students (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύται</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.291
			</span></i> tit. (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>that can be melted</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					193
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
